// @check
// The rule's SCOPE boundary, pinned so a later widening is a deliberate change
// rather than a surprise. `ping` and `pong` call each other on every path, so
// the pair diverges just as surely as a direct self-call — but the rule is keyed
// on the analysed declaration's OWN name, and neither function calls itself, so
// neither is flagged. Proving a mutual cycle needs a must-call graph over the
// whole module; direct self-recursion is the shape that has no other diagnostic
// at all. Zero diagnostics are asserted.
// `@check` only: calling either one would exhaust the stack.
function ping(n: i32): i32 {
  return pong(n + 1)
}
function pong(n: i32): i32 {
  return ping(n + 1)
}
print(ping(0))
